From 31e606514c9b694ecba7f94fce637f81841fe66c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SkillBuddy Agent <agent@skillbuddy.local>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 22:33:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Home heading alignment, fix unreliable dark-theme toggle,
 expand translation coverage
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Fixed Home welcome heading alignment: its container was missing the
  paddingHorizontal:16 that every other section on the screen uses,
  so the text sat flush against the screen edge while everything below
  it was indented — looked misaligned/broken. Fixed with a scoped
  inline override (the shared 'section' style is reused by 6 other
  blocks that already apply their own padding via sectionHeader, so
  changing it globally would have double-padded those instead).

- Fixed the 'sometimes dark mode just doesn't apply' bug: the previous
  implementation gated the actual setTheme() call behind an animation
  completion callback, guarded by an isAnimating ref that could get
  permanently stuck true if any callback misfired (interrupted
  animation, concurrent navigation, etc.) — silently blocking every
  future tap until the app was restarted. Rewrote so the theme change
  is now always synchronous and immediate on tap, completely decoupled
  from the cosmetic paint-reveal animation, which now also has its own
  safety-net timeout so it can never get stuck either.

- Substantially expanded translation coverage (EN/DE/ET/LV/LT): tab bar
  labels, Home (heading, quick-access tiles, all section titles, See
  All), Services (search placeholder, empty-state actions, header),
  Jobs (client/pilot view labels, filters, empty states, header),
  Profile (every menu item across both Client and Provider sections),
  and Settings (every label). Selecting a language now visibly changes
  a large majority of the app's most-seen text instead of just the tab
  bar and Home heading from the previous pass.

Full workspace typecheck: zero errors.

Not yet translated (follow-up): dynamic/interpolated strings (e.g.
'No services match "x"'), remaining sub-screens under Profile
(Documents, Wallet, Credit Points, FAQs, Legal, Safety), booking and
chat flows, and job posting/bidding screens.
